---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <span class="section-label">Live demo</span>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Watch an AI agent build a workflow out of real capabilities.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">This isn't a mockup. Your browser fetches the live Traverse capability registry, picks a group of related capabilities, and chains them into a real, working pipeline -- the same kind of workflow you could compose today with <code>traverse-cli</code>. Nothing on this page is precomputed or faked.</p>
      <div class="page-hero-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-accent badge-dot">Live registry data</span>
        <span id="discover-stats" class="badge">querying registry.traverse-framework.com…</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" id="discover-root">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="discover-graph-panel card">
      <div id="discover-graph" class="discover-graph-el"></div>
      <div class="discover-legend" aria-label="Graph legend">
        <span class="discover-legend-row">
          <span class="discover-legend-title">State</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-swatch is-idle"></span>Not used yet</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-swatch is-running"></span>Running now</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-swatch is-complete"></span>Completed</span>
        </span>
        <span class="discover-legend-row">
          <span class="discover-legend-title">Line</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-line is-dashed"></span>Discovery</span>
          <span class="discover-legend-item"><span class="discover-legend-line is-solid"></span>Data flow</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="discover-layout">
      <div class="terminal discover-terminal">
        <div class="terminal-header">
          <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="terminal-title" id="discover-phase-title">agent · discovering workflow</span>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-body discover-log" id="discover-log"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="discover-run-panel">
        <p class="t-body-sm t-muted"><strong>How to read it:</strong> your <strong>Goal</strong> is the request that starts everything. The <strong>Traverse system</strong> -- the AI agent, its MCP connection, and the runtime -- discovers and validates a matching workflow along the dashed line. The runtime then chains together the right <strong>capabilities</strong> to do the actual work, producing a <strong>Result</strong> along the solid line. Watch each step light up as it runs, and click any capability to open its real, published contract in the registry.</p>
        <button id="discover-run" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Discover another workflow →</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="discover-cards" id="discover-cards"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">How this is actually built</div>
      <h2>No server, no LLM call, no fixtures -- just the real catalog.</h2>
      <p>This page is static (Astro, no backend). On load, it fetches the same public <code>catalog.json</code> that powers the registry's catalog site, groups the current version of each capability by namespace, and orders any namespace with two or more active capabilities into a pipeline (ingest → interpret → decide → act) using a simple verb heuristic on each capability's name. That's the entire "agent" -- a composition heuristic running on live data, not a hosted model deciding anything. Once a workflow is composed, the graph steps each node through <strong>idle → running → completed</strong> to show execution order -- that sequencing is simulated in the browser, not a real invocation of the WASM binaries. Running a composed workflow for real is what <code>traverse-cli serve</code> is for. Click "Discover another workflow" to re-query the registry and see a different set of capabilities get composed.</p>
      <a href="/registry.html" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" style="margin-top:1rem">Browse the full registry →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title={"AI Agent Workflow Demo — Traverse Framework"}
  description={"See a real AI agent discover live capabilities from the Traverse registry and compose them into a working workflow -- right in your browser, no fixtures."}
  canonical={"https://traverse-framework.com/discover.html"}
  crumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">
    .discover-graph-panel { position: relative; padding: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
    .discover-graph-el { width: 100%; height: 460px; }
    .discover-legend {
      position: absolute; z-index: 5; right: 1.25rem; bottom: 1.25rem;
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
      background: var(--bg-elevated);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }
    .discover-legend-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; }
    .discover-legend-title { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--fg-subtle); font-size: 0.62rem; width: 32px; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .discover-legend-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; color: var(--fg-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
    .discover-legend-swatch { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; border: 2px solid transparent; }
    .discover-legend-swatch.is-idle { border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card); }
    .discover-legend-swatch.is-running { border-color: var(--accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 20%, transparent); }
    .discover-legend-swatch.is-complete { border-color: var(--success); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--success) 18%, transparent); }
    .discover-legend-line { width: 16px; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--fg-muted); }
    .discover-legend-line.is-dashed { border-top-style: dashed; }
    .discover-legend-line.is-solid { border-top-style: solid; }
    @media (max-width: 520px) { .discover-legend { right: 0.6rem; bottom: 0.6rem; left: 0.6rem; align-items: center; } .discover-legend-row { flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; } }
    .discover-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: stretch; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .discover-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .discover-graph-el { height: 520px; } }
    .discover-terminal { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
    .discover-log { flex: 1; max-height: 320px; overflow-y: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
    /* The terminal surface is a fixed dark editor background in both themes
       (matches .terminal / .code-block sitewide -- see components.css), so
       its text needs fixed colors too, not theme-reactive var()s that would
       flip to light-theme (dark-on-light) values and go unreadable here. */
    .discover-log-line { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #7d99a6; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .discover-log-line.cmd { color: #f2ecdf; }
    .discover-log-line.ok { color: #9ccdb2; }
    .discover-log-line.err { color: #e8907d; }
    .discover-log-line.accent { color: #debeef; font-weight: 500; }
    .discover-run-panel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); }
    .discover-cards { margin-top: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 0.85rem; }
    .discover-card { text-decoration: none; display: block; }
    .discover-card-top { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .discover-card-title { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    .discover-card-id { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    .discover-card-summary { line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
    .discover-card-link { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  </style>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/@antv/g6@5.1.1/dist/g6.min.js"></script>
  <script src="/assets/js/discover.js" defer></script>
</SubpageLayout>
